  "combos": {
    "combo1": {
      "title": "Havnis Extension through Herald of Orange Light",
      "description": "A prime example of Tearlaments' resilience to disruption. The opening Normal Summon of Tearlaments Reinoheart is met with the opponent's Infinite Impermanence, so the line plays out on their turn: Herald of Orange Light negates their Pumpking the King of Grave Ghosts, and Tearlaments Havnis Special Summons itself from the hand during their Main Phase. The resulting mills hit Tearlaments Merrli and Tearlaments Sulliek, netting a search for Tearlaments Scheiren and a Fusion Summon of Tearlaments Kitkallos, which extends into Tearlaments Rulkallos; Keldo the Sacred Protector then shuffles three of the opponent's Graveyard cards back into their Deck. Heads-up: this line uses Tearlaments Kitkallos and Agido the Ancient Sentinel, which are Forbidden in the TCG (as of 5 October 2026), so it isn't legal at TCG events as shown.",
      "date": "October 3, 2026",
      "credits": "✨ Replay by [AI] Tearlaments ✨",
      "formatVersion": 2,
